# Implementation Plan - Home Page Dashboard Dark Mode Styling

Fix the home page dashboard's dark mode compatibility issue. The dashboard cards, text, diagrams, and tables must adapt beautifully and legibly to dark mode, matching the premium visual style of the application.

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> The primary bug is that `:global(.dark)` is used in the standard global stylesheet `dashboard.css`. In standard CSS files, Next.js does not parse `:global(.dark)`, causing browsers to ignore the styles. Removing `:global()` and replacing it with simple `.dark` selectors will fully restore all dark mode styling variables.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The diagram elements (SVG text labels in Recharts) default to browser/system black colors. We will customize the `<Pie>` and `<Legend>` components to dynamically use the `isDarkMode` state so that text elements are fully legible and high-contrast on a dark background.

## Proposed Changes

### Dashboard Component & CSS

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard.css](file:///e:/Gravity/project-management_8/client/src/app/home/dashboard.css)
- Change all occurrences of `:global(.dark)` to `.dark` so the dark-theme CSS variables and class states are correctly registered by Next.js and interpreted by the browser.
- Set a default text color `color: var(--color-text-primary);` on the `.dashboard` container.
- Ensure `.custom-tooltip` explicitly sets its background to `var(--color-card)` and text color to `var(--color-text-primary)` to be legible in both modes.

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///e:/Gravity/project-management_8/client/src/app/home/page.tsx)
- Render custom SVG `<text>` elements in the Recharts `<Pie>` labels, setting the `fill` dynamically: `isDarkMode ? "#f3f4f6" : "#111827"`.
- Format the Recharts `<Legend>` items using the `formatter` prop, ensuring the text styles with standard Tailwind `text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-300 font-medium` for crisp visibility.
- Apply semantic CSS classes to `<CustomTooltip>` content to leverage the theme-aware colors correctly.

